		(uuid "09b3858d-3188-45ad-bf4a-96f124013e9f")
	)
	(text "XNANO J200 pin map (ATtiny416-XNANO edge connector)\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  pin  1 → VTG       (cut-strap modified, fed from VIN_5V)\n  pin  2 → PA0/UPDI  (mEDBG programming — not user-wired)\n  pin  3 → PA1       (mEDBG UART TX)         — NC on eval\n  pin  4 → PA2       (mEDBG UART RX)         — NC on eval\n  pin  5 → PA3       *** DIM control to U1 ***\n  pin  6 → PA4   ⚠ ATtiny412 lacks PA4 — DO NOT USE\n  pin  7 → PA5   ⚠ ATtiny412 lacks PA5 — DO NOT USE\n  pin  8 → PA6       (available; CSEL0 in target?)\n  pin  9 → PA7       (available; CSEL1 in target?)\n  pin 10 → PB5 ⚠ pins 10-19 are ATtiny416-only — DO NOT USE\n  pin 11 → PB4\n  pin 12 → PB3\n  pin 13 → PB2\n  pin 14 → PB1\n  pin 15 → PB0\n  pin 16 → PC0\n  pin 17 → PC1\n  pin 18 → PC2\n  pin 19 → PC3\n  pin 20 → GND\n\nFIRMWARE PORTABILITY: only PA0/1/2/3/6/7 are common to ATtiny412 and\nATtiny416 — restricting to these pins lets the SAME firmware build\ntarget both chips (toolchain: PlatformIO + megaTinyCore)."
